1
00:01,220 --> 00:05,200
Now let me go into each stage in more detail.

2
00:05,960 --> 00:08,220
Constructive Speeches - Details.

3
00:09,240 --> 00:12,940
1st speaker - your job is to lay the foundation.

4
00:13,720 --> 00:17,900
Clearly tell us your team's position and your main reasons.

5
00:18,760 --> 00:25,020
2nd speaker - your core job is to attack the opponent's 1st speaker's arguments.

6
00:25,620 --> 00:27,800
Find weaknesses in their logic.

7
00:27,800 --> 00:32,300
At the same time, support your own side with specific examples - real or hypothetical.

8
00:33,220 --> 00:36,620
So you are both a critic and a builder.

9
00:37,840 --> 00:39,520
Cross-examination.

10
00:40,260 --> 00:43,160
This is the question-and-answer round.

11
00:43,840 --> 00:49,540
First, the Affirmative 2nd and 3rd speakers question all Negative members.

12
00:50,240 --> 00:56,400
Then, the Negative 2nd and 3rd speakers question all Affirmative members.

13
00:57,180 --> 00:58,440
Important rules:

14
00:58,940 --> 01:02,080
The questioning side must control the pace.

15
01:02,580 --> 01:06,300
Decide how many questions to ask and when to switch.

16
01:06,900 --> 01:09,160
Because the total time is fixed.

17
01:10,140 --> 01:12,740
You may direct your question to a specific member.

18
01:13,360 --> 01:16,040
For example, "I'd like to ask the first speaker."

19
01:16,700 --> 01:21,640
However, the responding team is free to choose who answers.

20
01:22,200 --> 01:26,160
They are not forced to use the person you named.

21
01:27,340 --> 01:30,820
They can decide among themselves who is best suited to reply.

22
01:32,000 --> 01:35,460
We suggest that the two questioners take turns.

23
01:36,260 --> 01:39,100
For example, ask one or two questions each.

24
01:39,860 --> 01:41,900
But this is just a suggestion.

25
01:42,400 --> 01:48,620
If you find a strong line of attack, keep asking follow-ups without switching.

26
01:49,620 --> 01:53,020
Just don't interrupt each other, and watch the clock.

27
01:54,000 --> 01:56,560
Summary Speeches - 3rd speaker.

28
01:57,720 --> 01:59,500
This is your closing speech.

29
02:00,320 --> 02:03,120
Sum up your team's strongest arguments.

30
02:03,700 --> 02:10,920
Address the opponent's main challenges, and leave a memorable final impression.

